  "decision": "Raised the $5K estimate one point to 63% and held the $10K estimate at 31%. ETH held above the prior breakout near $2.77K, remained up 15.8% over seven days, and received $432.2M of broad-based U.S. spot ETF inflows across the two latest sessions. Rising staking, positive bridge flows, and stronger DEX activity add confirmation for the nearer target. Oil below $100 and a sub-5% U.S. 10-year yield provide tactical liquidity relief, but further central-bank tightening remains priced and the macro catalyst stays red. The Fed's improved discount-window operations are a stability backstop, not QE or a debasement turn. Direct L1 revenue remained small relative to application fees, and blockchain-neutral institutional rails do not establish ETH-specific value capture, so the $10K probability remains unchanged. No catalyst crossed a color threshold and no thesis-breaking event occurred."
